# Copy to `.env` and adjust. docker-compose and run.sh both read this file.
#
# This file is HOST IDENTITY (media paths, image pin, resource caps, creds) —
# machine-specific and uncommitted. METHODOLOGY knobs (rates, durations, warmup,
# noise floor, gate thresholds) live in the committed suite/bench.conf; anything
# set here or in the process environment overrides it (default < bench.conf < env).

# --- Jellyfin pin (MUST match the Jellyfin version whose OpenAPI spec you vendored) ---
# Pin by digest for byte-reproducible comparisons. Get one with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect jellyfin/jellyfin:10.11.8 --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}'
JELLYFIN_IMAGE=jellyfin/jellyfin:10.11.8
# JELLYFIN_IMAGE=jellyfin/jellyfin@sha256:...   # preferred: pin the digest

# --- Fair-comparison resource cap (identical for both servers) ---
BENCH_CPUS=4
BENCH_MEM=4g   # 2g OOM-kills ffmpeg on 4K HEVC transcode; identical for both either way

# --- Test data: the pinned real-library snapshot (recommended) ---
# BENCH_TESTDATA=1 seeds each server's config volume from suite/test_data/ (a
# read-only pinned snapshot of a real Jellyfin instance — see
# suite/snapshot-testdata.sh): Jellyfin boots it natively, Ferrofin adopts it.
# NO media is mounted at all; browse/query/user-data come from the database,
# images from the snapshot's metadata/ tree. Provisioning and scanning are
# skipped entirely (a scan over the absent media paths is the one thing that
# could diverge the two datasets). RUN_TRANSCODE must stay 0 in this mode: the
# snapshot's media files are deliberately not present.
BENCH_TESTDATA=1

# Never point the suite at real media. Any bind mount reaching /mnt/mangonas
# or /mnt/nvme0/k3s must be read-only (enforced by suite_assert_media_readonly
# and the post-start mount check — the run refuses to start otherwise).

# --- Synthetic padding (OPTIONAL) ---
# A real 20-movie library is thin for stressing the query/DTO path under load. Set these
# >0 to pad with synthetic items (tiny clips) and get query-scaling numbers.
FIXTURE_MOVIES=0
FIXTURE_SERIES=0
FIXTURE_EPISODES_PER_SERIES=10
# Music library: artists x albums x tracks (tagged flac). The PARITY leg (.env.loop) turns
# this on — the by-name music endpoints and the /Audio/* stream family need a real audio
# item. Off here: the perf leg registers no music library. NOTE both legs share
# fixtures/media; the first parity run regenerates the whole tree (the master clip gains a
# subtitle track + font attachment, series 01 becomes 30 s episodes), and the perf leg then
# measures that tree — expect to rebaseline perf/shape once after that.
FIXTURE_ARTISTS=0
FIXTURE_ALBUMS_PER_ARTIST=1
FIXTURE_TRACKS_PER_ALBUM=3
# Live TV fixture (M3U tuner + XMLTV guide; the PARITY leg turns it on). Off here: the
# measured perf fixture has no tuner.
FIXTURE_LIVETV=0
# The synthetic tree under fixtures/media is generated ONCE and shared by both legs, from
# whichever env triggers the generation: keep FIXTURE_MOVIES/SERIES/EPISODES_PER_SERIES
# equal here and in .env.loop, or the other leg runs on a differently sized library.

# --- Opt-in remote subtitles (parity leg) ---
# With all three set, the parity leg installs the OpenSubtitles plugin on Jellyfin,
# configures both servers, and runs the remote-subtitle journey (needs the internet).
#OPENSUBTITLES_USERNAME=
#OPENSUBTITLES_PASSWORD=
#OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY=

# --- Load profile ---
# The per-endpoint comparison legs are OPEN-LOOP (constant arrival rate) and
# configured in suite/bench.conf (BENCH_RATE*, BENCH_DURATION_SECS, warmup,
# login storm). Only the deliberately closed-loop legs still use VUs:
BENCH_VUS=50             # phase C (contention) + pool-sweep client population
BENCH_DURATION=30s       # closed-loop legs' window

# --- Deterministic admin creds (both servers seeded with these) ---
BENCH_ADMIN_USER=bench
BENCH_ADMIN_PASSWORD=benchpass123

# --- Transcode time-to-first-segment ---
# MUST stay 0 with BENCH_TESTDATA=1: the snapshot's media files are
# deliberately absent, so there is nothing to transcode (open item in the plan).
RUN_TRANSCODE=0
TTFS_ITERATIONS=3        # cold play-starts measured per mode (copy + encode)
TTFS_BITRATE=8000000     # encode-mode MaxStreamingBitrate; far below the 4K source forces a real re-encode
